  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 141 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nWednesday night through Monday\nAssessment...a certainty (>98%) of much cooler conditions for\nthe first part of the weekend. Probability of frost Friday night\nhas increased to 60-70%.\n\nThe next round of rain with embedded thunderstorms will occur \nWednesday night into Thursday evening. A tropical connection with \nthe Gulf and moisture coming off of Simon will increase PWATs into \nthe 1.5 to 2 inch range. These PWAT values have the potential of \nmeeting or exceeding the climatological max for October 15th. Thus \nheavy rainfall is a given. The area currently favored for the heavy \nrain is south of I-80.\n\nVery windy conditions will be seen late Thursday night and Friday \nbehind the cold front. Winds atop of the mixed layer are 30-35 knots \nwhich would give wind gusts to at least 35 mph on Friday. We will \ncontinue to watch this for potential headlines.\n\nCold Canadian high pressure will settle over the area Friday night \nbringing light winds and very chilly temperatures. Given the \nnegative delta on temperatures, the probability of frost has \nincreased to 60-70 percent. Headlines for frost are expected later \nin the week.\n\nA warm-up commences late this weekend into early next week with \ntemperatures trending to and then above normal.",
